      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;Rich Dad Poor Dad&quot; is based on Robert Kiyosaki&apos;s upbringing in Hawaii and how his education and experiences shaped his views on money, life, and work. The book contrasts the approaches of two men from different backgrounds—one wealthy and one poor—and how their methods influenced Kiyosaki&apos;s key life decisions. It covers important topics such as the value of financial knowledge, the tax advantages of businesses, and how wealth is measured by the number of days your income can sustain you without working. Through these lessons, the book emphasizes financial independence and how different approaches to teaching these principles can lead to very different outcomes in life.</marc:subfield>
